  "recorded-file-input-url": {
    "content": [
      {
        "text": "This is **Warren Buffett’s 2024 annual letter to Berkshire Hathaway shareholders**, dated **February 22, 2025**. The 15-page file contains the letter plus two pages comparing Berkshire’s stock performance with the S&P 500—not the full annual report.\n\n### What’s inside\n\n- **2024 financial results:** Berkshire reported **$47.4 billion in operating earnings**, up from **$37.4 billion in 2023**, driven largely by stronger insurance results and investment income. Nevertheless, 53% of its 189 operating businesses reported lower earnings.\n- **Investment strategy:** Buffett explains Berkshire’s preference for owning good businesses over holding cash, despite its large cash position. Its marketable equity holdings ended the year at **$272 billion**, down from $354 billion.\n- **Insurance operations:** A discussion of GEICO’s improvement, catastrophe risks, disciplined pricing, and Berkshire’s **$171 billion in insurance “float”**—money held before claims are paid.\n- **Japanese investments:** Berkshire’s stakes in **ITOCHU, Marubeni, Mitsubishi, Mitsui, and Sumitomo** cost $13.8 billion and were worth **$23.5 billion** at year-end. Buffett expects these to remain long-term holdings.\n- **Management and succession:** Reflections on admitting and correcting mistakes, selecting managers, and **Greg Abel’s expected succession as CEO**.\n- **A tribute to Pete Liegl:** The story of Berkshire’s acquisition of Forest River and its founder’s contributions.\n- **Taxes and reinvestment:** Buffett reports **$26.8 billion in U.S. federal income-tax payments** for 2024 and discusses how retained earnings and compounding helped build Berkshire.\n- **Annual meeting information:** Plans for the **May 3, 2025 gathering in Omaha**, including the Q&A schedule and shareholder shopping events.\n\n### Performance tables at the end\n\n| Measure | Berkshire | S&P 500, including dividends |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 2024 return | 25.5% | 25.0% |\n| Compounded annual gain, 1965–2024 | 19.9% | 10.4% |\n\n**Overall:** It combines a business update with Buffett’s lessons on long-term investing, honest management, risk, and reinvesting profits.",
        "type": "text"
      }
    ],
